---
// Standard ATS-friendly CV (English) — Strict 1-Page A4 Linear Single-Column
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Federico Colombo - Resume (ATS)" description="ATS-optimized 1-page resume for Federico Colombo - Technical Artist & Real-Time Graphics Engineer" />
		<style>
			@page {
				size: A4 portrait;
				margin: 0;
			}
			* {
				box-sizing: border-box;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				font-variant-ligatures: none !important;
				font-feature-settings: 'liga' 0, 'clig' 0, 'calt' 0 !important;
				letter-spacing: normal !important;
				text-align: left;
			}
			body {
				font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
				background-color: #f1f5f9;
				color: #1f2937;
				line-height: 1.32;
				-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
				print-color-adjust: exact;
			}
			.controls {
				text-align: center;
				padding: 14px 20px;
				background-color: #131416;
				border-bottom: 1px solid #272a32;
				color: #eceae4;
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				gap: 12px;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
			}
			.controls a {
				background-color: #181a1e;
				color: #eceae4;
				border: 1px solid #3a3f4b;
				padding: 8px 15px;
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
				text-decoration: none;
				border-radius: 3px;
				font-weight: 600;
			}
			.controls a.primary {
				background-color: #e09f3e;
				border-color: #e09f3e;
				color: #131416;
			}
			.document {
				width: 210mm;
				height: 297mm;
				max-height: 297mm;
				margin: 24px auto;
				background-color: #ffffff;
				padding: 10mm 14mm 8mm 14mm;
				box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
				overflow: hidden;
			}
			.cv-header {
				border-bottom: 1.5px solid #0f172a;
				padding-bottom: 5px;
				margin-bottom: 6px;
			}
			h1.cv-name {
				font-size: 17.5pt;
				font-weight: 800;
				color: #0f172a;
				line-height: 1.1;
				margin-bottom: 2px;
			}
			.cv-role {
				font-size: 9pt;
				font-weight: 700;
				color: #1e3a8a;
				margin-bottom: 3px;
			}
			.cv-meta-line {
				font-size: 7.5pt;
				color: #334155;
				line-height: 1.35;
			}
			.cv-meta-line a {
				color: #1e40af;
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 600;
			}
			h2.cv-section-title {
				font-size: 8.6pt;
				font-weight: 800;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: #0f172a;
				border-bottom: 1px solid #94a3b8;
				padding-bottom: 1.5px;
				margin-top: 6.5px;
				margin-bottom: 3.5px;
			}
			.summary-text {
				font-size: 7.65pt;
				line-height: 1.32;
				color: #1f2937;
			}
			.skills-row {
				font-size: 7.55pt;
				line-height: 1.30;
				margin-bottom: 2px;
				color: #1f2937;
			}
			.skills-row strong {
				color: #0f172a;
			}
			.entry-item {
				margin-bottom: 5px;
			}
			.entry-item:last-child {
				margin-bottom: 0;
			}
			.entry-header {
				font-size: 8pt;
				font-weight: 700;
				color: #0f172a;
				line-height: 1.24;
				margin-bottom: 1.5px;
			}
			.entry-meta {
				font-size: 7.45pt;
				font-weight: 500;
				color: #475569;
			}
			.entry-link {
				font-size: 7.45pt;
				font-weight: 700;
				color: #1e40af;
				text-decoration: none;
			}
			.entry-bullets {
				list-style: disc;
				padding-left: 14px;
			}
			.entry-bullets li {
				font-size: 7.55pt;
				line-height: 1.29;
				margin-bottom: 1.4px;
				color: #1f2937;
			}
			@media print {
				body {
					background-color: #ffffff;
					margin: 0;
				}
				.controls {
					display: none !important;
				}
				.document {
					margin: 0;
					box-shadow: none;
					width: 210mm;
					height: 297mm;
					max-height: 297mm;
					padding: 10mm 14mm 8mm 14mm;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="controls">
			<a href={`${baseUrl}/Federico Colombo - Resume (Standard).pdf`} download="Federico_Colombo_Resume_ATS.pdf" class="primary">Download ATS PDF (1-Page)</a>
			<a href={`${baseUrl}/cv-ats-it`}>Versione Italiana (ATS)</a>
			<a href={`${baseUrl}/cv`}>Visual Web CV</a>
			<a href={baseUrl}>Back to Portfolio</a>
		</div>

		<div class="document">
			<header class="cv-header">
				<h1 class="cv-name">FEDERICO COLOMBO</h1>
				<div class="cv-role">Technical Artist &bull; Real-Time Graphics Programmer &bull; Pipeline &amp; XR Engineer</div>
				<div class="cv-meta-line">
					Turin, Italy (Open to EU Relocation &amp; Remote CET) &bull; Italian / EU Citizen &bull; +39 351 307 8191 &bull; <a href="mailto:colombofederico28@gmail.com">colombofederico28@gmail.com</a><br />
					Portfolio: <a href="https://federicocolombo12.github.io/PortFolio/">federicocolombo12.github.io/PortFolio</a> &bull; GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/federicocolombo12">github.com/federicocolombo12</a> &bull; LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/federico-colombo10">linkedin.com/in/federico-colombo10</a>
				</div>
			</header>

			<section>
				<h2 class="cv-section-title">PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY</h2>
				<p class="summary-text">
					Technical Artist and Real-Time Graphics Programmer completing an M.Sc. in Cinema &amp; Media Engineering at Politecnico di Torino (Expected: December 2026, 110/110 Cum Laude; B.Sc. 100/110). Combines low-level C++17/OpenGL 3.3 and WebGPU/WGSL rendering pipelines with Unity 6 (URP/SRP), Unreal Engine 5, Python DCC tooling, and mobile XR optimization. Cut GPU frame time by 61.3% (7.52ms to 2.91ms) at locked 90 FPS with 0B per-frame GC allocations in PulseEngine on Meta Quest 3, built a 15-dispatch WebGPU 2D GI compute pipeline, and mentored 60+ engineering students as Teaching Assistant.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="cv-section-title">TECHNICAL SKILLS</h2>
				<div class="skills-row"><strong>Languages &amp; Shaders:</strong> C++17, C#, Python 3, HLSL, GLSL, WGSL, TypeScript/JavaScript, Shader Graph, Unreal Material Editor</div>
				<div class="skills-row"><strong>Engines &amp; Graphics APIs:</strong> Unity 6 (URP, SRP Batcher, Compute Shaders, OpenXR, UPM, EditorWindow), Unreal Engine 5 (PCG, Niagara, MetaHumans, Alembic Groom, Live Link, Sequencer, C++/Blueprints), OpenGL 3.3, WebGPU</div>
				<div class="skills-row"><strong>Rendering &amp; Profiling:</strong> Deferred Shading (G-Buffer), Cook-Torrance PBR, Raymarching &amp; SDFs, Jump Flooding (JFA), Mikkelsen Surface Gradients, Silhouette POM, 3D Gaussian Splats, RenderDoc, NVIDIA Nsight Graphics, Unity Profiler</div>
				<div class="skills-row"><strong>DCC, Pipeline &amp; Color:</strong> Blender (bpy scripting), Autodesk Maya, RealityCapture, DaVinci Resolve (ACES/OCIO), OpenUSD, Git / Git LFS, CMake, CI/CD</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="cv-section-title">PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE</h2>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Technical Artist &amp; Producer (XR Master Thesis R&amp;D — PulseEngine) <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Lemons in the Room &amp; Politecnico di Torino &bull; Florence / Remote &bull; 03/2026 – Present</span></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Architected a bio-adaptive volumetric raymarching framework in Unity 6 URP and HLSL compute shaders for Meta Quest 3, locking 90 FPS on standalone mobile hardware.</li>
						<li>Cut GPU frame time by 61.3% (7.52ms down to 2.91ms) and maintained 0B per-frame GC allocations via Dynamic Bounding Volumes, adaptive ray stepping, and compute shader voxelization.</li>
						<li>Authored Morten Mikkelsen Surface Gradient shaders on SDF volumes to remove triplanar UV seams, built custom Unity Editor telemetry tooling (DAWMixerWindow), and packaged the system as a UPM module.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Technical Artist, Gameplay Programmer &amp; Project Lead <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Level Up Lab (PoliTo Student Team) &bull; Turin, Italy &bull; 11/2024 – 07/2026</span></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Established 2D/3D art pipelines across <em>Spicy Mercante</em> and <em>Line Operator</em>, defining sprite atlasing, sorting layers, polycount budgets, naming conventions, and Git LFS workflows for a 6–7 developer pod.</li>
						<li>Authored custom HLSL shaders (animated water vertex displacement, dynamic cutaways), C# asset validation editor utilities, and Blender 3D asset pipelines while profiling draw calls and batching across milestones.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Software Developer &amp; AI Consultant <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Intellecto IP &bull; Turin, Italy / Remote &bull; 06/2026 – Present</span></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Engineered a React personal banking dashboard consolidating 4+ banking API feeds, and automated 15+ weekly operational workflows via Anthropic Claude LLM toolchains and Notion API integrations.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Teaching Assistant — Graphical User Interfaces &amp; Media Systems <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Politecnico di Torino &bull; Turin, Italy &bull; 10/2024 – 01/2025</span></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Mentored 60+ engineering students in weekly laboratory sessions on UI architecture, frontend performance, and structured debugging workflows, authoring technical guides and exercises.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Video Artist &amp; Technical Camera Operator <span class="entry-meta">&bull; RKH SRL &bull; Turin, Italy &bull; 09/2023 – 06/2024</span></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Operated cinema cameras (RED, Blackmagic), studio lighting grids, camera tracking plates, and DaVinci Resolve color grading pipelines (ACES/Rec.709).</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="cv-section-title">KEY PROJECTS</h2>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Graphics Lab Engine (C++17, OpenGL 3.3, GLSL, CMake, RenderDoc) <span class="entry-meta">&bull;</span> <a class="entry-link" href="https://github.com/federicocolombo12">GitHub</a></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Built a custom C++17 deferred shading renderer from scratch with G-Buffer packing, Cook-Torrance PBR BRDF, Tangent-Space Silhouette Parallax Occlusion Mapping (SPOM), and RenderDoc frame inspection.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">WebGPU 2D Global Illumination Compute Lab (TypeScript, WGSL, 512x512 Float16) <span class="entry-meta">&bull;</span> <a class="entry-link" href="https://github.com/federicocolombo12/webgpu-2d-gi-jfa">Repo</a> <span class="entry-meta">&bull;</span> <a class="entry-link" href="https://federicocolombo12.github.io/webgpu-2d-gi-jfa/">Live</a></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Authored 8 hand-written WGSL shaders across a 15-dispatch compute pipeline: Jump Flooding SDF, 16-ray Monte Carlo sphere tracing with 1-bounce indirect GI, temporal EMA, shared-memory Bloom, and AgX Pass Inspector.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">Smart Cable Generator &amp; Stylized 3D Gaussian Splats (Python bpy, OpenUSD, EEVEE-Next) <span class="entry-meta">&bull;</span> <a class="entry-link" href="https://github.com/federicocolombo12/Blender-Smart-Cables-Generator">Cables Repo</a></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Developed a Blender Python add-on for distance-proportional catenary cables with automated UV/FBX export, plus an NPR 3DGS shader pipeline via OpenUSD PointClouds and Geometry Nodes Kuwahara filtering.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>

				<article class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">UE5 Technical Art Studies (PCG, Niagara, MetaHumans, Alembic Groom, Live Link) <span class="entry-meta">&bull;</span> <a class="entry-link" href="https://federicocolombo12.github.io/PortFolio/">Portfolio</a></div>
					<ul class="entry-bullets">
						<li>Built spline-driven PCG terrain with slope/altitude auto-materials, multi-emitter Niagara curl-noise VFX, and MetaHuman Alembic groom physics with ARKit Live Link Face mocap.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="cv-section-title">EDUCATION</h2>
				<div class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">M.Sc. in Cinema &amp; Media Engineering (Class LM-32) <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Politecnico di Torino &bull; Oct 2024 – Dec 2026 (Expected, 110/110 Cum Laude)</span></div>
				</div>
				<div class="entry-item">
					<div class="entry-header">B.Sc. in Cinema &amp; Media Engineering (Class L-8) <span class="entry-meta">&bull; Politecnico di Torino &bull; Oct 2021 – Jul 2024 (Final Grade: 100/110)</span></div>
				</div>
				<div class="skills-row" style="margin-top: 2px;"><strong>Languages:</strong> Italian (Native), English (Fluent / C1), French (Basic), German (Basic)</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>
